module bindings.rust.symlink_resolution_without_base_containment;

// The standard library documents the two halves of safe symlink handling
// separately. Path::is_symlink reports that a path points at a link;
// Path::canonicalize resolves the link and returns the target as an absolute
// path; fs::symlink_metadata reads a path's own metadata without following
// it. None of those three says anything about where the target lands: a link
// planted inside a tree that is served, listed or walked resolves to wherever
// it points, and every reader that goes through it -- the metadata call, the
// file open, the entry's listing row -- reads outside the tree.
//
// The documented way to allow links while keeping a tree rooted is the
// component-wise comparison family on Path: starts_with and strip_prefix
// compare whole path components against a base, and components and ancestors
// walk them. Refusing links outright needs no resolution at all, which is why
// the binding requires the resolution half: code that only tests is_symlink
// and stops -- the detector that reports a link for its caller to refuse, the
// filter that skips link entries -- never reaches for the target and is not
// this shape. What is reported is the function that has already decided a
// path may be a link, resolves or inspects the target anyway, and carries no
// component-wise containment against a base directory.
//
// The judgement lives in the pack rule; this binding only recognises the
// atoms. Every clause is an exact-token match over the resolving function's
// own context tokens, so prose in a comment satisfies neither side and a
// sibling function's containment comparison cannot clear the resolution.

binding symlinkResolutionWithoutBaseContainment {
  query pattern presenceNode where node.scope == "function" and node.context.language == "rust" and node.context.call in ["is_symlink"] and node.context.call in ["canonicalize", "symlink_metadata"] and not (node.context.call in ["starts_with", "strip_prefix", "components", "ancestors"])
  emit issue code.SymlinkFollowedWithoutBaseContainment at node
}
